**New evidence**
Sharif’s coalition and social-safety team framed welfare as a governing objective early in 2022, with explicit references to poverty reduction, human capital, women, health, education, malnutrition, and data-driven delivery.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"SCO International Forum for Poverty Alleviation is a great effort, Shazia Marri","publisher":"PID / Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-05-26","url":"https://pid.gov.pk/site/press_detail/19910","claim":"The poverty-alleviation ministry said the present government was using data, technology, financial inclusion, women’s empowerment, human-capital formation, and reduced barriers to health and education to build a welfare state.","locator":"keynote address text, 26 May 2022","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct government statement by the responsible minister in 2022; rhetoric is explicit, though implementation still needs corroboration.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within Sharif’s 2022 ruler-period.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Sharif-led federal government through its poverty-alleviation ministry; it reflects stated policy intent more than measurable delivery.","contrary_evidence":["This is mainly an intent statement and does not by itself prove implementation or outcomes."],"lenses":["6B.1","6B.2","6B.3","6B.4","6B.5","6B.8","6B.9","6B.10"]}

The federal health agenda in mid-2022 included a World Bank-financed push to widen equitable access to primary care, especially for women and children in underserved districts.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Bank Supports Primary Healthcare and Universal Coverage to Strengthen Human Capital in Pakistan","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-06-07","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/06/06/-world-bank-supports-primary-healthcare-and-universal-coverage-to-strengthen-human-capital-in-pakistan","claim":"The World Bank approved $258 million for Pakistan’s National Health Support Program to strengthen primary health care and accelerate universal health coverage, with emphasis on communities lagging behind and on access for children and women during pregnancy and childbirth.","locator":"press release lead and program summary","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank press release with concrete financing and program design details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and under the Sharif government.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Sharif-led government’s health policy environment, but financed and implemented with provincial and donor participation.","contrary_evidence":["World Bank financing is not the same as Sharif personally designing or executing the program."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.4","6B.9","6B.10"]}

Women’s and maternal nutrition was another explicit policy focus, again with an equity and service-delivery framing rather than a generic growth narrative.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan Maternal Nutrition Strategy 2022-27","publisher":"UNICEF Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-05","url":"https://www.unicef.org/pakistan/reports/pakistan-maternal-nutrition-strategy-2022-27","claim":"UNICEF and the Government of Pakistan set a strategy to protect and promote diets, practices, and services supporting women’s health and well-being, with evidence-based and equity-based nutrition programmes at scale for preconception, pregnancy, and postpartum periods.","locator":"Highlights and strategy objectives","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Joint UNICEF-government strategy document with clear program goals and target groups.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Sharif-era federal government working with UNICEF; implementation was shared with health systems and provinces.","contrary_evidence":["This is a strategy document rather than proof of nationwide delivery in 2022."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.4","6B.5","6B.8"]}

Health-system modernization was also being piloted through a basic-package approach that aimed at more equitable access and stronger provincial localization.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Towards sustainable financing for PHC and UHC: The piloting of Essential Package of Health Services in Pakistan","publisher":"WHO","publication_date":"2022-05-18","url":"https://www.who.int/news-room/feature-stories/detail/bringing-support-phc-sustainable-health-financing-together-pakistan","claim":"WHO said Pakistan had approved a limited national Essential Package of Health Services for immediate district-level implementation and had localized the package into provincial plans and budgets in all provinces except Punjab by May 2022.","locator":"overview and 'Moving planning to results' sections","source_type":"official/IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"WHO feature story describing a concrete health-policy pilot and the status of localization in 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target period.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Pakistan health system under the Sharif government; WHO and donors were co-implementers, so attribution is shared.","contrary_evidence":["The story describes piloting and partial localization, not full national implementation."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.4","6B.5","6B.9","6B.10"]}

A separate poverty-alleviation initiative was described as part of the prime minister’s vision and targeted poorer households with interest-free loans.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PR No.53","publisher":"PID / Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-05-14","url":"https://pid.gov.pk/site/press_detail/19807","claim":"The finance minister said the Kamyab Pakistan Program was consistent with Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif’s vision to improve living standards and would provide interest-free loans to poorer segments through a bottom-up approach.","locator":"meeting summary, 14 May 2022","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct government press release naming the program, purpose, and beneficiary design.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and Sharif’s first months in office.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Sharif-led federal government through the finance ministry; this is an intent-and-design source more than a delivery audit.","contrary_evidence":["The release does not establish whether the program materially improved incomes in 2022."],"lenses":["6B.1","6B.2","6B.3","6B.7","6B.10"]}

When floods struck, Sharif personally directed fast cash relief through BISP with electronic transfer and a transparent process.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif directed to ensure the provision of Rs. 50,000 relief to each flood affected family through a transparent process within the three days","publisher":"PID / Government of Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-08-15","url":"https://pid.gov.pk/site/press_detail/20561","claim":"The prime minister directed that every flood-affected family receive Rs. 50,000 within three days, with BISP cash relief delivered under NDMA supervision and via electronic transfer so deserving people would get relief.","locator":"PR No. 135, 15 August 2022","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct PM instruction recorded in the official press release with concrete amount, mechanism, and delivery timeline.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 flood emergency.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Shehbaz Sharif as prime minister; operational delivery still depended on BISP, NDMA, and provincial machinery.","contrary_evidence":["This was emergency relief, not a durable reform of ordinary welfare provision."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.3","6B.6","6B.7","6B.10"]}

